# 320: §6 `.46` — the bodies of if/else/while are ALWAYS braced, so there is no
# dangling-else question and an unbraced body is a parse error, at the line of the
# token that was found (2). Nothing runs, so line 1's `print` produces nothing.
--- source
print 1;
if true print 2;
--- expect
error: Parse at line 2: expected '{', found 'print'
